# Build output
/pingularity
/dist/

# Runtime data
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Scratch artifacts from local testing - these have been committed by accident
# before (two copies of /bin/sleep and a saved curl response), so they are
# named explicitly rather than trusted to discipline.
busybin*
r.json

# Local, machine-specific helper scripts
deploy.sh

# Private engineering notes - the public posture lives in docs/security-model.md
.notes/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Agent scratch: workflow worktrees are created here at runtime and are not
# part of the product. They are real git worktrees, so an unguarded `git add -A`
# commits them as embedded repositories.
.claude/
/compose.yaml

# Credential shapes. Unlike the scratch-artifact block above, this one is not a
# scar: no file matching these patterns is tracked, and nothing in the tree
# generates or writes key material - there is no key generation, no x509 and no
# PEM encoding in any .go file here. It is purely preventative. It earns its
# place because `git add -A` sweeps every one of these paths in today, and a
# secret pushed to a public repo is the one accident a follow-up commit cannot
# undo - the credential has to be rotated instead. Cheap to carry, irreversible
# to omit.
.env
.env.*
.envrc
.netrc
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# Local build and profiling artifacts. Preventative too: nothing in the tree
# produces them today - CI runs plain `go test ./... -count=1 -race`
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml:58) and `node --test internal/web/ui/*.test.mjs`
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml:61), with no coverage or profiling flag on any `go
# test` line in .github/ and no npm/yarn/pnpm step anywhere in it. These are just
# the default output names a local `go test -c`, `-coverprofile` or `-cpuprofile`
# run leaves behind, listed so an afternoon of profiling cannot ride along in
# someone's commit. node_modules/ is the same bet on a future `npx`: there is no
# package.json today.
coverage.out
*.test
*.prof
node_modules/
